MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Low Country Blues feels like a natural next choice after Memphis and Old Sock because I want more of that earthy, blues-centered sound.",
    "Croz fits the reflective songwriting and familiar rock sound I am drawn to alongside You Should Be So Lucky; it feels worth choosing today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Jake Bugg's folk-rock direction is less appealing right now because I am looking for familiar blues and classic rock rather than exploring that sound.",
    "The live DVD/CD package and extensive archival recordings interest me musically, but they feel like a larger listening commitment than I want today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in classic rock seems to have been taken as a strong interest in lengthy live collections, although those are not what I want this visit.",
    "Acoustic or roots-oriented music is not automatically a next choice for me; Lighthouse and Jake Bugg do not have the same immediate pull as Low Country Blues."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The strongest connection for me now is the earthy blues feeling of Memphis and Old Sock, which makes Low Country Blues especially compelling.",
    "I only choose a couple of albums on a visit, so finding Revelator or Blak and Blu appealing does not mean I would choose them today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in blues and familiar rock, but gave too much weight to related live collections and too little to my immediate listening priorities."
}
